Psalms 46:10.display_text:
The rulers of peoples gathered with Abraham’s God;
for the mighty of the earth belong to God;
they were greatly exalted.

Psalms 21:16.display_text:
My strength dried up like a potsherd;
my tongue is stuck to my throat,
and Thou broughtest me down into the dust of death.

Isaiah 55:1.display_text:
You who thirst, go to the water;
and you who have no silver, go and buy wine and rich food,
and drink without silver or price.

Psalms 74:9.display_text:
For in the Lord’s hand is a cup
of unmixed wine, full of mixture;
and He tilted from this into that,
but its dregs were not emptied out;
all the earth’s sinners will drink.

Psalms 136:6.display_text:
May my tongue cling to my throat
if I do not remember you,
if I do not set Jerusalem first at the beginning of my gladness.

Psalms 78:1.display_text:
A psalm for Asaph.
God, nations entered Thine inheritance;
they defiled Thy holy temple;
they made Jerusalem into a fruit-watchman’s hut.
